    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Symptoms and state of health",
     "texto": [
      "To describe a cold, expressions such as «ik ben verkouden» (I have a cold) and «ik hoest» (I cough / I have a cough) are used. «Koorts» is fever («Heeft u koorts?»). To ask whether the condition is getting worse, the comparative adjective «erger» (worse) is used: «Wordt de hoest erger?» (Is the cough getting worse?)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
